    "Candid scope of bean qou-ys29 (zero fitting): (1) Because |PSL(2, 7)| = 168 does not divide |Aut(Sigma_Bring)| = |S_5| = 120 (7 !| 120, gcd(120, 168) = 24), PSL(2, 7) is NOT a subgroup of Bring's automorphism group S_5. What is proved algebraically and representation-theoretically here is the exact S_4 maximal-subgroup bridge (Stab_{S_5}(pt) ~= S_4 of index 5 and Stab_{GL(3,F_2)}(pt) ~= Stab_{GL(3,F_2)}(line) ~= S_4 of index 7), the faithful irreducible embedding of all 168 elements of PSL(2, 7) as Blichfeldt's finite subgroup G_168 inside SU(3)_c, and the exact Lie-derivation cutdown dim Der(O) = 14 (g_2) -> dim Stab_{Der(O)}(e_7) = 8 (su(3)_c). (2) What remains open in moduli / surface geometry is proving that pinching an S_4-invariant cycle on Bring's genus-4 curve and normalizing produces a genus-3 curve whose automorphism group enhances from S_4 to the Hurwitz maximum PSL(2, 7) (the Klein quartic), and constructing the smooth manifold coset G_2 / SU(3)_c ~= S^6 beyond Lie-algebra tangent spaces."
